---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GuideArticle from '../../components/v2/templates/GuideArticle.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../../data/images';
import { getPageSEO } from '../../utils/seo';

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'Does Karinderya support co-op?', answer: 'Yes. The official Roblox description calls Karinderya a co-op restaurant simulator.' },
  { question: 'How many players can share a server?', answer: 'Third-party Roblox metadata reports a six-player server cap, but this guide does not treat that as a permanent creator promise.' },
  { question: 'Are Cash, inventory, and progress shared?', answer: 'The official description does not document those rules. Check them in the current game before planning a shared session.' },
  { question: 'How are Workers different from teammates?', answer: 'Players coordinate directly with one another. Use the Workers Hub for information about Worker support inside restaurant management.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout pageId="guides-co-op-guide" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }, { label: getPageSEO('guides-co-op-guide').h1 }]}>
<GuideArticle
  title={getPageSEO('guides-co-op-guide').h1}
  kicker="Team play guide"
  intro="Karinderya officially supports co-op play, while ownership, shared resources, and progression rules still require current in-game confirmation."
  tableOfContents
  heroImage={siteImages.beginnerGuideHero}
  nextPage={{ label: 'Cooking and Serving Guide', href: '/guides/cooking-and-serving/' }}
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Workers Hub', href: '/workers/', description: 'Review Worker support as a separate restaurant-management topic.' },
    { label: 'Beginner Guide', href: '/guides/beginner-guide/', description: 'Learn the complete restaurant service loop.' },
    { label: 'Cooking and Serving Guide', href: '/guides/cooking-and-serving/', description: 'Follow an order through preparation and service.' },
    { label: 'Restaurant Layout Guide', href: '/guides/restaurant-layout/', description: 'Keep team movement routes easy to follow.' },
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="does-karinderya-support-co-op">Does Karinderya Support Co-op?</h2>
  <p>Yes. SILOG’s official Roblox description identifies Karinderya as a “Co-op Restaurant Simulator.” That confirms multiplayer as part of the game, but it does not define shared Cash, inventory, restaurant ownership, rating, Worker access, or host progression.</p>

  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>Players join through Roblox’s multiplayer environment. Public Roblox metadata reported by third-party trackers shows a six-player server capacity, but server capacity alone does not prove that all six players share every restaurant system.</p>

  <h2 id="how-it-works">What Players Can Do Together</h2>
  <p>The official listing confirms the co-op format. Dated gameplay also shows players present in the restaurant environment, but the exact permissions for cooking, serving, building, and management have not been documented by the developer. Treat the current prompts as the authority for what a guest can do.</p>

  <h2 id="team-planning-process">Team Planning Process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Review the restaurant workflow together.</li>
    <li>Identify the active customer, kitchen, serving, and supply tasks.</li>
    <li>Choose a temporary focus for each player.</li>
    <li>Use short messages when an order or work area needs attention.</li>
    <li>Change focus when another part of the restaurant becomes harder to manage.</li>
    <li>Reduce active work when the team loses track of the current tasks.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="team-roles">Team Roles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Dining area:</strong> keep customer-facing tasks visible.</li>
    <li><strong>Kitchen:</strong> follow preparation and cooking tasks.</li>
    <li><strong>Serving:</strong> connect prepared food with the dining area.</li>
    <li><strong>Supplies:</strong> review ingredient needs when service allows.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These are planning labels, not mandatory game roles. Change them whenever the current restaurant needs a different arrangement.</p>

  <h2 id="shared-systems">What Is Shared</h2>
  <p>Shared Cash, inventory, Workers, rating, restaurant ownership, and saved progress are not confirmed by the official description. Test these systems with the current host and guests before making purchases or assuming that an action affects every player.</p>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use clear messages when handing a task to another player.</li>
    <li>Keep the kitchen and dining route easy for teammates to read.</li>
    <li>Finish visible work before increasing the number of active tasks.</li>
    <li>Use the Workers Hub when comparing player coordination with Worker support.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="common-mistakes">Common Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Having several players follow the same task.</li>
    <li>Keeping one team arrangement when the restaurant needs change.</li>
    <li>Moving Furniture or Equipment without telling teammates.</li>
    <li>Assuming every group should divide work in the same way.</li>
  </ul>

  <FAQ slot="faq" items={faqItems} />
</GuideArticle>
</BaseLayout>
